{"id": "LUA-01", "type": "luau", "question": "Write a Luau ModuleScript named Inventory in --!strict mode. Export a type `Inventory = { [string]: number }`. Provide `Inventory.new(): Inventory`, `Inventory.add(inv: Inventory, itemId: string, count: number): ()` which raises an error if count is not a positive integer, `Inventory.remove(inv: Inventory, itemId: string, count: number): boolean` which returns false and changes nothing when the inventory holds fewer than count (and removes the key when the count reaches 0), and `Inventory.count(inv: Inventory, itemId: string): number`.", "expected": ["content/en-us/luau/type-checking.md", "src/content/docs/types/tables.md", "content/en-us/scripting/module.md"]}
